We need to consider the company's performance: EPS up 22% YoY, but revenue down 17% due to lower gasoline price. Gasoline margin high, but overall revenue down. Same-store sales modest growth (1-2%). Operating expenses up modestly, but cost reductions offset. Cash flow $129M, capex $75M. Debt down. Store count expanding, acquisitions.

