**3. Operational performance and volume growth** – Transport volumes in the natural‑gas segment were up 8% YoY, with Texas volumes up 4% and crude/condensate up 8%. The firm also added 2.3 Bcf of long‑term firm capacity in Q4, bringing total new commitments to ~4 Bcf for the year. Refined‑product volumes grew 3.8% YoY, outpacing the modest 0.5% growth in U.S. demand. These volume trends indicate that the asset base is being utilized more fully and that the company is capturing higher‑margin export opportunities (LNG, Mexico).  

