- Net income rose 52% YoY to $21.5 M, marking the 27th consecutive quarter of record earnings.  
- The 39% loan‑book increase since September 2014 includes $544 M (16%) attributable to the Virginia Heritage merger; organic loan growth in Q3 2015 was only 5% ($226 M).  
- Deposit growth (39% over 12 months) also contains a sizable merger component (21% organic).  

**2. Robust profitability metrics, yet some dilution**  
