We have limited data: revenue down 13% YoY, adjusted EBITDA up from $27M to $33M (increase). They talk about restructuring, exiting coal tar, focusing on chemicals, etc. Some positive: performance chemicals strong, safety improvements, but overall revenue decline, reliance on CM&C segment which is being reduced. Need to assess outlook: they are cutting capacity, exiting coal tar, focusing on higher margin chemicals, but near term revenue pressure, credit facility changes, leverage covenant.

