1. **Revenue and earnings momentum** – Q3 site‑rental revenue rose 7% YoY to $765 million, with $43 million of organic growth (≈6% YoY). Adjusted EBITDA and AFFO both beat the high‑end of the prior guidance, indicating operating performance is stronger than expected.

2. **Guidance upgrade** – Management raised the full‑year 2015 outlook at the midpoint for site‑rental revenue (+$60 million), adjusted EBITDA (+$37 million) and AFFO (+$23 million). The updated AFFO per‑share target of $4.30 reflects an 8% YoY increase, and 2016 AFFO per‑share is also projected to grow 8% to $4.66.

