**3. Macro headwinds** – Management highlighted “headwinds in our Advanced Markets” tied to global trade tensions, softening consumer‑electronics demand, tariffs and the Huawei ban. They expect these pressures to **continue into Q3**, which is why the Q3 revenue outlook is **lower than Q2** ($450‑$465 million versus $474 million). This signals a near‑term drag on top‑line growth.  

**4. Long‑term growth narrative** – The company points to a **34% CAGR** in Advanced Markets over the 2014‑2018 period (vs. a 4% market growth rate) and a **20% CAGR** in the semiconductor business (vs. a 9.7% WFE CAGR). Non‑GAAP EPS has grown >50% CAGR over the same span, indicating a strong historical track record of out‑pacing its markets.  

