Rationale:  

**Positive indicators**  
- **Earnings per share** rose 22% YoY to $0.66, and six‑month EPS increased 38% to $1.53, showing strong bottom‑line growth despite a weaker top line.  
- **Gasoline margin** remains a key driver: $14.03 /gal versus $13.07 /gal a year ago, marking 9 of the last 10 quarters with a margin above $0.12/gal. This high‑margin fuel business cushions overall profitability.  
- **Margin expansion in core retail categories** – grocery/general merchandise margin up 20 bps to 34.1%, prepared‑food/fountain margin up 400 bps to 64.2% – indicates effective cost control and product mix improvements (e.g., lower cheese cost, expanded coffee offerings).  
