| **Capital allocation** | Ongoing stock‑buyback (up to $2 M) signals confidence in current valuation, but also reduces cash available for strategic investments. | May boost short‑term EPS, but limits flexibility if larger acquisition or R&D needs arise. |
| **Risks / uncertainties** | • Small absolute scale – earnings are $1.3 M, leaving little cushion for a miss.<br>• Dependence on a handful of vascular products; competitive pressure in stent‑graft market.<br>• Upcoming cash outflows for UnBalloon earn‑out and potential US product launches.<br>• Guidance not provided in the excerpt; forward‑looking statements are limited. | The company remains vulnerable to a slowdown in hospital spending, product‑launch setbacks, or higher operating costs. |
