- One-time tax charge $4.4B (including $3.3B repatriation tax, $1.1B DTA remeasurement). Effective tax rate reduction to ~24%.

- Excluding charge, Q4 net earnings $2.5B, EPS $5.68. Including charge, loss $1.9B, EPS -$5.51.

- Full year 2017: net revenues $32.1B up 5% YoY. Including charge, net earnings $4.3B EPS $9.01. Excluding charge, net earnings $8.7B up 17% YoY, EPS $19.76 up 21%. Return on average common equity 10.8%, book value per share up 5% YoY.

- Investment Banking strong: net revenues $2.1B Q4, up 19% QoQ; underwriting up 55% QoQ; full year IB net revenues $7.4B up 18% YoY; leading positions in M&A and equity underwriting.

- Institutional Client Services (ICS) weak: Q4 net revenues $2.4B down 24% QoQ; full year $11.9B down 18% YoY; FICC down.

- Overall diversified model, but some segments under pressure.

- Mention of investments in engineering, growth initiatives, future tailwinds from tax reform (potential increased M&A, financing).

- The one-time tax charge is a drag but excluded shows strong earnings growth.

- Need to assess outlook: tax reform may boost activity; IB backlog up; but macro environment uncertain; FICC pressure continues.

- As of Jan 2018, Goldman Sachs had solid capital ratios, but need to consider valuation, dividend, share buybacks, etc. Not provided.

- As a financial analyst, we can weigh the strong IB growth and potential tailwinds vs weakness in FICC and overall market volatility.

