We need to parse the content: It's MarineMax (boat retailer). They report same-store sales growth 10% Q3, year-to-date 23% growth. Margin improvement but gross margin down slightly due to mix shift. SG&A up modestly, benefit costs increase. Net income up 16% to $13.3M, EPS $0.52 vs $0.47. Pretax earnings doubled. Cash $47M, inventory up 10% but turns improving. No tax expense due to NOLs. Borrowings up modestly.

Overall positive growth, but some concerns: margin pressure from used boat mix, SG&A increase, benefit costs, inventory increase, reliance on NOLs for tax shield, industry mixed performance, weather risk.

