analysisWe need to produce decision: 0 for Buy, 1 for Sell, 2 for Hold. Provide rationale based on earnings call content. Summarize key points: earnings per share modest increase, weather impact lowered gas demand, but offset by fuel cost recovery, lower O&M, regulatory amortization freeze, lower interest costs, higher electric sales to large customers, growth in connections, construction projects (biomass plant, air quality upgrades), renewable portfolio compliance, large capital projects, fuel diversity, low natural gas prices, shift to gas, reduction in coal usage.

Assess outlook: positive operational improvements, but earnings modest, weather risk, capital expenditures high ($245-255M biomass, $900M air quality). Need to consider balance sheet, cash flow, dividend, regulatory environment. Not provided. But we can infer: lower O&M, lower interest, but high capex may pressure cash flow. However, they have regulatory freeze base rates for 2012, which helped O&M. They reaffirm full-year forecast despite lower gas demand. That suggests confidence.

