**2. Guideline upgrades** – Management raised the midpoint of its full‑year 2015 outlook for site‑rental revenue (+$60 m), adjusted EBITDA (+$37 m) and AFFO (+$23 m). The AFFO per‑share target is now $4.30, an 8% increase versus 2014, and 2016 AFFO per share is projected at $4.66 (another 8% lift). Raising guidance in the same quarter that already beat expectations signals confidence in continued momentum.

