- **Margin and cash‑flow beat:** Operating margins came in ahead of plan, driven by better gross margins and lower overhead. Normalized EPS benefited from pricing, mix and productivity. Operating cash flow swung to a positive $191 million, up $180 million YoY, and management raised its full‑year cash‑flow outlook.  
