- **Margin pressure risk** – The discussion of “investing in inventory to meet unparalleled demand” hints at a build‑up of stock. Under Armour has historically struggled with inventory excess and margin compression, especially as it expands into footwear and international markets where it faces higher cost structures and pricing pressure.

- **Competitive landscape** – Footwear production is projected at 30 million pairs versus competitors’ ~500 million. While this underscores growth potential, it also signals that Under Armour is a small player in a highly capital‑intensive, brand‑driven segment dominated by Nike and adidas. Scaling up without sacrificing margin will be challenging.

