**1. Underlying earnings strength despite a one‑time tax hit**  
- The $4.4 bn one‑time charge (mainly deemed repatriation tax) pushed Q4 GAAP EPS to –$5.51, but on an adjusted basis earnings were $2.5 bn and EPS $5.68.  
- For the full year, adjusted net earnings rose 17% YoY to $8.7 bn, EPS up 21% to $19.76, and ROE was 10.8% – solid profitability for a diversified investment bank.  

