We need to consider the content: Newell Brands Q2 2019 results. They claim progress on turnaround, core sales growth in 4 of 7 divisions, operating margins ahead of plan, operating cash flow positive $191M vs -? previous year, cost reductions, SKU reductions, SAP conversions, divestitures, debt reduction $777M, etc. However need to consider overall outlook, risks, sustainability, growth prospects, margin improvement, cash conversion, portfolio strength, but also note that only 4 of 7 divisions delivering growth, still early, need to expand, reliance on cost cuts, potential for further divestitures, and macro environment.

