We have a transcript of Polaris (likely Polaris Industries) Q2 2015 earnings call. Key points: record sales $1.124B, EPS $1.49. 11% revenue growth, strong motorcycle demand, Slingshot strong, Asia-Pacific and Latin America robust, EMEA weak. Operating expense growth below 6% for first time in >5 years. However, paint issues at Spirit Lake causing high costs, need to fix. They are holding and narrowing full-year guidance. Expect better margins in H2 due to pricing, lower commodity costs, productivity gains. Expect Fed rate hikes not to materially impact. They discuss five-year strategy, growth via innovation and acquisitions, mention Multix vehicle for Indian market. They talk about gross margin expansion 300-500 bps over next five years. Overall positive tone but some concerns: paint issues, higher costs, inventory management, macro uncertainty (China). Guidance narrowed.

